==================================================
1. KEEP THE CURRENT TRANSFORM MODEL
==================================================

The current architecture is now useful groundwork:

    rigSelectedIdx     = canonical active part
    rigXform           = move | rotate | scale
    rigAxis            = x | y | z | null
    +/-                = applies the selected transform

Do not redesign this.

Do not merge rigSelectedIdx with rigPickIdx.

Do not change rig data semantics.

==================================================
2. MAKE THE TOOLBAR HONEST
==================================================

The current toolbar visually risks implying that selecting:

    MOVE
    ROTATE
    SCALE
    X / Y / Z

lets the user manipulate the model directly in the viewport.

It does not.

For now these are NUDGE controls.

Adjust labels/tooltips/microcopy so the interaction is obvious:

    choose transform mode
    choose axis
    use + / - to nudge

Do not make it look like a Blender gizmo until viewport dragging actually
exists.

Keep the compact toolbar.

==================================================
3. ADD CLICK-AND-HOLD REPEAT TO + / -
==================================================

Currently +/- performs one step per click.

Make pointer hold repeat the nudge.

Desired behaviour:

    pointerdown
        apply one step immediately

    short delay (~250-350ms)

    while held
        repeat at a comfortable rate (~60-100ms)

    pointerup
    pointercancel
    pointerleave
        stop repeating

Mouse and pen should work through pointer events.

Do not create runaway timers.

Always clean up the interval/timeout.

A normal quick click should still produce exactly ONE nudge.

==================================================
4. KEEP EXISTING STEP SIZES
==================================================

Do not tune transform semantics in this pass.

Preserve the current values:

    MOVE     1 unit
    ROTATE   5 degrees
    SCALE    0.1

Preserve:

    axis selected -> affect that axis
    no axis       -> existing all-axis behaviour

Do not change stored fields or generator interpretation.

==================================================
5. DO NOT KEY AUTOMATICALLY
==================================================

Nudging is editing the current structural/pose values.

Do not silently create keyframes merely because +/- was held.

Existing explicit KEY behaviour remains explicit.

Pose-then-key can come later.

==================================================
