RigWorld then maps that identity to:

    rigSelectedIdx

Do not implement it now.

==================================================
7. RECORD THE FUTURE PICKING CONTRACT
==================================================

Add a concise nearby TODO/comment if useful, but no implementation.

The future implementation should follow these rules:

A. Pointer coordinates MUST use:

    renderer.domElement.getBoundingClientRect()

NOT:

    window.innerWidth
    window.innerHeight

because the viewport occupies only part of the browser window.

B. Raycast only explicit model pickables.

Do not raycast indiscriminately against:

    grid
    lights
    camera helpers
    bounds helpers
    future transform handles

C. The pick result must resolve to a stable rig-part identity.

Do not depend solely on arbitrary Three child ordering.

Preferred eventual metadata:

    object.userData.rigPartIdx

or another explicit stable identifier attached when the shared viewport builds
the object.

Then:

    onPick(identity)
        ->
    RigWorld / RIG workspace
        ->
    setRigSelectedIdx(...)

D. onPick must be OPTIONAL.

Existing script/shared viewport callers that do not provide it must behave
exactly as before.

==================================================
8. IMPORTANT FUTURE DESIGN NOTE
==================================================

When viewport picking is implemented, do NOT stop at:

    onPick(mesh.name)

unless inspection proves names are guaranteed unique and stable.

The research proposes onPick(name), which is directionally correct, but the
better contract is an explicit identity owned by the source object.

For RIG that ideally means:

    rig part index
or
    stable rig part id

attached as userData to the rendered root/group.

A model filename/name may not uniquely identify a part because the same model
can legitimately be used by multiple body parts.

Example:

    ARM_L -> ARM.MOD
    ARM_R -> ARM.MOD

Picking ARM.MOD must still identify which arm was clicked.

Design for that when the picking pass happens.

